  "_comment": "Model names, in two tiers. `ship` is what a starter or example may pin: a developer clones that code and is evaluating CopilotKit on whatever it names, so it has to be a model we would choose today. `recognize` is every other real name, which documentation may mention -- a migration note, a comparison, a model a reader already runs. Adding a name to `recognize` is routine. Moving one into `ship` is a decision about what we put in front of a new developer. Reviewed 2026-09-16; a list of current models goes stale by sitting still, so revisit it when a provider ships a tier.",
